    {
      "description": "The cookie_value is decoded and passed directly to pickle.loads on line 7. The cookie is user-controlled external input; deserializing untrusted pickle data can result in arbitrary code execution (RCE), data loss, or other critical impacts. This is a security-sensitive deserialization flaw. Static scan (AST_DANGEROUS_PICKLE_LOAD high) confirms the unsafe pickle.loads call. Replace pickle with a safe serialization format (e.g., JSON) and sign/verify the cookie; do not deserialize untrusted input.",
      "category": "injection",
      "severity": "critical"
    }
  ],
  "decision": "REJECT",
  "fix_description": "Critical: unsafe pickle.loads of user-controlled cookie allows RCE. Fix plan: replace pickle with safe JSON serialization and add HMAC signature/verification (using a server secret) to prevent tampering. Specifically: in load_cached_profile, base64-decode cookie, verify the HMAC signature before trusting the payload, then json.loads; in save_cached_profile, json.dumps and sign with HMAC; get_theme remains unchanged except that it uses the secure loader. Handle invalid/missing cookie data gracefully by returning {} / default preference. This is a security-sensitive change and requires human approval before applying; treat as L2 risk and do not auto-merge.",
